#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""Gaming VM telemetry for Walter's Prometheus (see hypervisor/gaming/README.md, "Telemetry").

Runs on the hypervisor as the operator (group libvirt), as the systemd --user unit gaming-exporter.service.
Every INTERVAL seconds a background thread collects:
  - gpu-mode's state file and whether a game-mode/ai-mode switch is running;
  - the host CPUs that system.slice, user.slice and init.scope may use;
  - linux-gaming's libvirt stats (`virsh domstats`, never the libvirt Python bindings);
  - while linux-gaming runs: one ssh call into the guest (nvidia-smi, Sunshine, stream check).
and renders Prometheus text. HTTP requests only ever get that cached text: no request runs a command.

  GET /metrics   the cached exposition text        GET /healthz   200 "ok" while collection is current
Anything else is 404. Listens on ${HYPERVISOR_BRIDGE_IP}:9188 (IP_FREEBIND, so the bridge may come up
later); the nft table inet gaming_exporter_guard (gaming-setup.sh, step exporter) lets only Walter in.

Everything the guest prints is untrusted: it is read with a size cap, parsed strictly (numbers only, in
range, the GPU name reduced to [A-Za-z0-9 ._-]), and anything else is dropped.

Python 3 stdlib only. Optional environment (e.g. in ~/.config/deck/gaming-exporter.env, see the unit):
  GAMING_EXPORTER_BIND   ADDR:PORT to listen on instead of ${HYPERVISOR_BRIDGE_IP}:9188 (tests, smoke runs)
  GAMING_GUEST_USER      the guest account to ssh into (default: ssh's own, i.e. ~/.ssh/config or $USER)
  GAMING_GUEST_KEY       the guest ssh key (default ~/.ssh/id_linux_gaming)
  GAMING_SUNSHINE_PORT   Sunshine's base port, its `port` setting (default 47989)
  SITE_ENV               site values file (default ~/.config/deck/site.env; read, never sourced)
"""

